 To make the given code more efficient, I would suggest the following steps:

1. Fetch prompts data only once at component mount and store it in a ref or useMemo for reusage. This will reduce the number of API calls.

```javascript
const promptsData = useMemo(() => api.prompt.all.useQuery().data, []);
```

2. Use the `useEffect` hook to call `utils.prompt.invalidate()` after successful mutations instead of calling it inside each mutation's `onSuccess` callback. This way, we avoid making unnecessary API calls.

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  if (upsertPrompt.isSuccess || deletePrompt.isSuccess) {
    utils.prompt.invalidate();
  }
}, [upsertPrompt.isSuccess, deletePrompt.isSuccess]);
```

3. Memoize the `setInputMessage` function to prevent unnecessary renders when setting the message.

```javascript
const setInputMessageMemo = useCallback((message) => {
  setInputMessage(prevState => ({ ...prevState, message }));
}, [setInputMessage]);
```

4. Use the `useMemo` hook to memoize the sorted prompts array to avoid recalculating it on every render.

```javascript
const sortedPrompts = useMemo(() => {
  return promptsData?.sort((a, b) => b.updatedAt.getTime() - a.updatedAt.getTime());
}, [promptsData]);
```

5. Remove unnecessary `api.prompt.all.useQuery()` dependency from `upsertPrompt` and `deletePrompt` mutations as they don't need it.

